course: dictionary
lesson: 10760
title: Usable: able to be used
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Usable means able to be used, or in a good enough state to be used. Look at its parts: use, and able. Something usable works, or is good enough to do its job. «It is a great story, but DNA breaks down over time, and after 66 million years no usable dinosaur DNA is left.» The clues are breaks down over time and no usable DNA is left. The DNA is damaged so much that it can no longer be used.
explain: Usable is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as a tool, a room, some space or some water. It can also be spelled useable, and both spellings are correct. Ask yourself: could someone actually use this right now? If yes, it is usable. If it is broken, worn out or too damaged, it is not.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «No dinosaur DNA that can be used is left» still makes sense, so usable has the right meaning here. Usable does not mean old or famous. It only asks whether something can be used.
fact: Usable means able to be used, or in a good enough state to be used.
fact: Usable can also be spelled useable, and both spellings are correct.
fact: «Usable space» means room you can actually use, not space that is blocked or full of junk.
fact: «Usable water» means water clean and safe enough to use.
fact: The opposite of usable is unusable: a broken tool or a flooded room cannot be used.
exercise: What does usable mean? | Very large and wide | Easy to lose | Very old and worn out | *Able to be used, or good enough to use
exercise: «After the flood, only three rooms were usable.» What does usable mean here? | Empty and locked | Painted in bright colours | Full of water | *Able to be used
exercise: Ella asks, «Is useable spelled differently from usable?» What is the answer? | *Both spellings are correct and mean the same | Useable means very old | Useable is wrong, always write usable | They mean opposite things
test: «No usable dinosaur DNA is left.» What does this tell you about the DNA? | It is famous | *It is too damaged to be used | It is the best kind of DNA | It is brand new
test: Which word means the opposite of usable? | *Unusable | Reusable | Useful | Helpful
exam: Why does the author write «no usable dinosaur DNA is left»? | Because dinosaur DNA is very large | Because DNA is found in every rock | Because the story is funny | *Because the DNA is too damaged to be used
